%N A399544 Number of unlabeled Ferrers relations on an n-element set.
%C A399544 A relation R is Ferrers if xRy and zRw imply xRw or zRy.
%C A399544 Two Ferrers relations R and S on an n-element set are considered equivalent if there is a permutation p of the underlying set such that (x,y) is in R if and only if (p(x),p(y)) is in S.
%H A399544 J. Christophe, J.-P. Doignon and S. Fiorini, <a href="https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/journals/JIS/VOL6/Doignon/doignon40.html">Counting biorders</a>, Journal of Integer Sequences, Vol. 6 (2003), Article 03.4.3.
%F A399544 a(n) = (1/n!)*Sum_{k=0..n} |Stirling1(n,k)|*A048163(k+1), where |Stirling1(n,k)| denotes the unsigned Stirling number of the first kind.
%e A399544 a(3) = (2*A048163(2) + 3*A048163(3) + A048163(4))/3! = (4 + 42 + 230)/6 = 46.
%Y A399544 Cf. A048163 (labeled Ferrers relations).
%K A399544 nonn,new
%O A399544 0,2
